This license applies to AiBridge Host (AiBridgeHost.exe) and AiBridge Host
Connect (AiBridgeHostConnect.exe), version 0.9.0 and later, together with the
apps bundled in them. The source code is not published and is not licensed to
you.

AiBridge Host runs on a PC: it serves web apps, connects to a telescope mount
(LX200 serial/TCP, ASCOM Alpaca, INDI, N.I.N.A., or a built-in simulated
mount) and exposes an AiBridge-compatible device API. The AiBridge ESP32
firmware is a separate project under the MIT License
(https://github.com/OnStepNinja/AiBridge). Optionally, AiBridge Host Connect
lets an AI assistant (such as claude.ai or Grok) create and test apps and,
with your approval, operate connected equipment.

PERMITTED, free of charge, no registration or payment required:
- Downloading this software and running it, in unmodified form, for your own
  personal or organizational astronomy use.
- Placing your own web apps in the apps folder and using them with this
  software, including apps written with the help of an AI assistant. You own
  the apps you write.

