⚠ PROTOTYPE SOFTWARE: this is an early prototype (v0.9.0), still under
development and released to gather feedback. It may not work correctly and
may behave unexpectedly, including with connected hardware (telescope mount).
- It opens a local web server. By default it accepts connections from this PC
  only. Web pages from other sites are refused, and an optional PIN can
  protect access from other devices. However, apps that you open from the
  server run outside its approval system: such an app can send commands to the
  connected mount (slew, park, stop, change settings), can use the server's
  administration functions, and may be able to send data to the internet.
  Use only apps you trust or have read. Enable LAN access only on a network
  you trust.
- AI features are experimental. An AI assistant can write apps and, after you
  accept a warning, can send commands to connected equipment; GOTO, sync and
  settings changes require your approval each time. AI-written apps and
  AI-sent commands can be wrong. Test first on the simulated mount; on real
  equipment, test carefully, one small movement at a time.
- Using the AI features involves your AI provider's service and a temporary
  public tunnel (Cloudflare Quick Tunnel). You are responsible for the
  accounts, plans and networks you use them with.
- Stay with the equipment, keep STOP within reach, and be ready to cut power.
  Unattended operation is not supported.

